  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Watching, Waiting shows clear signs of active use, with 1,660 recorded downloads and open access availability through a hybrid distribution model. Its strongest recorded signals are practical and policy-relevant: the book aligns with Good health and well-being and carries funding verification from KU Leuven and the Institute of Art History. Citation uptake is not yet visible in the available record, so its impact story is currently one of early dissemination and topical relevance rather than documented scholarly accumulation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Watching, Waiting, published by Leuven University Press in 2023, is an interdisciplinary scholarly book that examines emptiness, photography, and place in the wake of Covid-19 while also reaching beyond that immediate moment. The record suggests a work positioned at the intersection of architecture, anthropology, sociology, and public health concerns, with a conceptual link to Good health and well-being and a broader sustainability and policy relevance signal. That combination points to a book whose themes are resonating not only as cultural analysis but also as a contribution to contemporary discussions about place, absence, and social life.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The clearest evidence of reach is usage: the book has been downloaded 1,660 times in the available OAPEN metrics. That pattern indicates steady reader interest and suggests the work is being accessed as part of the open scholarly infrastructure. Open access availability through the repository record strengthens that reach by lowering barriers for readers in research, teaching, and professional contexts.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Other signals support the book\u2019s scholarly standing. The record shows peer-review metadata from the publisher context, and the book is associated with funding verification from KU Leuven and the Institute of Art History. Those details do not measure influence directly, but they do indicate institutional support and a formal publication pathway, both of which can aid uptake over time.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At this stage, the citation record remains quiet, with no citations visible in OpenAlex. That should be read cautiously: for a recent book, citations often emerge later than downloads and other forms of engagement. The available evidence therefore points to a work that is already being read and accessed, with its longer-term scholarly influence still developing.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, Watching, Waiting is best described as an openly available, institutionally supported scholarly book with demonstrable reader attention and clear thematic relevance to current debates about health, place, and social environments. Its impact is currently strongest in dissemination and interdisciplinary relevance, while formal citation-based influence has not yet accumulated in the record.</p>",
